## MissingRenderPartialArguments

**Severity:** error | **Type:** LiquidHtml | **Aliases:** `MissingRenderPartialParams`

This check ensures that all required `@param` arguments declared in a partial's `{% raw %}{% doc %}{% endraw %}` tag are provided at the call site. It helps you catch missing required arguments at development time rather than at runtime. `{% raw %}{% render %}{% endraw %}`, `{% raw %}{% include %}{% endraw %}` and `{% raw %}{% function %}{% endraw %}` call sites are all checked, and each offense names the tag you actually wrote.

A parameter is considered required when it is declared without square brackets around its name in the `{% raw %}{% doc %}{% endraw %}` tag (e.g. `@param {string} name` is required, `@param {string} [name]` is optional).

The `{% raw %}{% doc %}{% endraw %}` tag is treated as the contract: a parameter it declares as required must be passed, even if the partial happens to supply its own fallback with the `| default` filter. If a parameter is genuinely optional, mark it as such in the `{% raw %}{% doc %}{% endraw %}` tag rather than relying on the fallback — [RequiredDocParamWithDefault](/developer-guide/platformos-check/checks/required-doc-param-with-default) reports the partials where the two disagree, so the fix lands on the file that can make it.

This check only runs when the target partial has a `{% raw %}{% doc %}{% endraw %}` tag. For partials without a `{% raw %}{% doc %}{% endraw %}` tag, see [PartialCallArguments](/developer-guide/platformos-check/checks/partial-call-arguments).

An `{% raw %}{% include %}{% endraw %}` site is bound by the contract too, even though `include` runs the partial in the caller's scope and the value could therefore be inherited. A declared parameter is a declared parameter: if the partial is meant to read the name from its caller rather than receive it, do not declare it. For an included partial with no `{% raw %}{% doc %}{% endraw %}` tag, where the parameter list can only be guessed at, the finding is a warning from [ImplicitIncludeArguments](/developer-guide/platformos-check/checks/implicit-include-arguments) instead.

## Examples

### &#x2717; Incorrect Code Example (Avoid using this):

```liquid
{% raw %}
{% comment %}app/views/partials/user/card.liquid{% endcomment %}
{% doc %}
  @param {string} name - The user's display name
  @param {string} [avatar_url] - Optional avatar URL
{% enddoc %}
<div class="card">
  <h2>{{ name }}</h2>
</div>
{% endraw %}
```

```liquid
{% raw %}
{% comment %}Calling site — required 'name' argument is missing{% endcomment %}
{% render 'user/card', avatar_url: user.avatar %}
{% endraw %}
```

### &#x2713; Correct Code Example (Use this instead):

```liquid
{% raw %}
{% render 'user/card', name: user.name, avatar_url: user.avatar %}
{% render 'user/card', name: user.name %}
{% endraw %}
```

The same applies to `{% raw %}{% function %}{% endraw %}` call sites:

```liquid
{% raw %}
{% comment %}Error — required 'name' argument is missing{% endcomment %}
{% function card = 'user/card' %}

{% comment %}OK{% endcomment %}
{% function card = 'user/card', name: user.name %}
{% endraw %}
```

## Configuration

The default configuration for this check:

```yaml
MissingRenderPartialArguments:
  enabled: true
  severity: error
```

## Disabling This Check

Disabling this check is not recommended. If a parameter is truly optional, mark it with square brackets in the `{% raw %}{% doc %}{% endraw %}` tag: `@param {string} [param_name]`.

